  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The specific heat capacity of a substance in the solid state is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"c\"></span> and the specific latent heat of fusion of the substance is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span>. When <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5000\"></span> J of energy is supplied to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> kg of this substance in the solid state, the temperature of the substance increases by <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span> K. When <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"20000\"></span> J of energy is supplied to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{m}{2}\"></span> kg of this substance in the solid state at its melting point, the substance completely melts without a change in its temperature. What is the ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{c}{L}\"></span>?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.010\"></span> K</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.0025\"></span> K</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.010\"></span> K<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.0025\"></span> K<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
